    "blurb": "Features a standout Dark Star > Eyes Of The World sequence with Jerry’s crisp lead and Phil’s booming bass, plus a soaring Bird Song. Playing In The Band and Me And My Uncle deliver high‑energy moments in the first set, while the second set maintains strong momentum. Overall the show is solid with clear stage‑mix capture.",
    "review": "Assembly Hall on Feb 22 1973 captures the Dead in a tight groove, rolling from a punchy first set into one of the year’s most memorable second sets. Jerry’s guitar shines throughout – his laser‑like leads drive the Dark Star > Eyes Of The World stretch, while his tone stays crystal clear on Bird Song and Playing In The Band. Phil “bombs” with a powerful, melodic bass that underpins the jams and adds vocal depth, especially on Box of Rain. Keith weaves jazzy counterpoint that lifts the improvisations, and Bill’s drumming locks the rhythm in place, propelling the band forward during the high‑energy moments. The stage‑mix matrix feed cleaned up by Charlie Miller delivers a full‑show picture with clear vocals and minimal dropouts, making this performance both accessible and rewarding for listeners.",
